The commandtypedefcan also be used with more complex types. For example,
the following code gives the namevifor a vector of integers, and the namepifor
a pair that contains two integers.
typedefvector<int>vi;
typedefpair<int,int>pi;
MacrosAnother way to shorten code is to definemacros. A macro specifies that
certain strings in the code will be changed before the compilation. In C++, macros
are defined using the#definekeyword.
For example, we can define the following macros:
#defineF first
#defineS second
#definePB push_back
#defineMP make_pair

